cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the exact public GitHub commit for this review-pending research disclosure."
title: "The proper hat-guessing number of K5-e"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "Protti"
    given-names: "Matthew"
version: "0.1"
date-released: 2026-09-02
repository-code: "https://github.com/matthewprotti/planar-ssuf-four-terminal-bound/tree/hgp-k5e-v0.1-review-pending/research/proper_hat_guessing_k5_minus_e"
abstract: >-
  We prove that the proper hat-guessing number of the complete graph on five
  vertices with one edge removed is eight. The lower bound uses an explicit
  construction over F_2^3 and Hall's theorem; the upper bound follows from the
  general vertex/chromatic-number bound.
keywords:
  - hat guessing
  - proper coloring
  - graph theory
  - Hall's theorem
  - finite geometry
  - AI-assisted mathematics
